ile":"discovery","protocol_version":"1.0.0","python_implementation":"CPython","python_version":"3.11.15","separation_policy":{"binding_energy_source":"src/elementzero/physics/conversion.py::binding_energy_MeV","definitions":{"S2n":"S2n(Z,N) = B(Z,N) - B(Z,N-2)","S2p":"S2p(Z,N) = B(Z,N) - B(Z-2,N)","delta2n":"delta2n(Z,N) = S2n(Z,N) - S2n(Z,N+2) = 2*B(Z,N) - B(Z,N-2) - B(Z,N+2)","delta2p":"delta2p(Z,N) = S2p(Z,N) - S2p(Z+2,N) = 2*B(Z,N) - B(Z-2,N) - B(Z+2,N)"},"derivation_rule":"ez-b003-derived-observable-v1: S2n, S2p, delta2n, and delta2p are algebraic combinations of the binding energies used to compute them, and those binding energies are algebraic combinations of mass excesses. A derived observable is not independent evidence from its inputs: it re-expresses them. Atlas facts for these quantities carry derived = true, independent_evidence = false, and the exact input identities.","derived":true,"independent_evidence":false,"observables":["S2n","S2p","delta2n","delta2p"],"separation_policy_id":"ez-b003-separation-observables-v1","shell_indicator_caveat":"A large positive local change in delta2n or delta2p is consistent with shell structure; it is not proof of a magic number. No local maximum is promoted to a closure claim, and no p-value is reported without a preregistered null model.","training_rule":"No model is trained on a derived target. Models predict mass excess; binding energy and every separation observable are computed afterwards.","units":"MeV"}},"evidence_protocol_version":"0.3.0","model_ids":["EZ-BSKG3-TABLE-v1","EZ-BSKG3-TABLE-v1+GP-RESIDUAL-v1"],"not_evaluable":[],"profile":"discovery","protocol_version":"1.0.0","raw_source_hash":"e8599c6d7f724fac91934e59f1b9de8fb8f63e820f4b39456b790665ed2a3307","scope":"real-evaluated-data-wo14","scope_rule":"The criterion answers one narrow question: was known shell-related mass structure rediscovered under controlled masking? Meeting it is not evidence for any predicted new closure, and not evidence for an island